  "raw_text": "41\n\nBapi mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto set up and put in place, to stand up and put in place, to set up and install, to establish\n \n/\nestablecer y poner en su lugar, ponerse de pie y poner en su lugar, establecer e instalar, establecer\n\nLâ bapaia daknika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \njudicial committee\n \n/\n \ncomité judicial\n\nBara\n \n–\n \nand\n \n/ y, e\n\nBâra\n \n(Bara)\n \n(short form of / forma corta de:\n \nBahara\n)\n \n–\n \nthere, therein, thereon, to that place\n \n/ allí, ahí, al respecto, a ese\nlugar\n\nBâra sa\n \n–\n \nthere is, there are\n \n/ hay, ahí esta\n\nBarli\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbarley\n \n/\n \ncebada\n\nBarli\n \nm\nâ\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbarley grain\n \n/\n \ngrano de cebada\n\nBas\n \n(\nv\n-\nimp\n \no\nf\n/de:\n \nK\naia\n)\n \n–\n \nbe\n \n/\n \ns\né\n, sea, sean\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nK\narna bas\n \n–\n \nbe strong\n \n/\n \nsé fuerte\n)\n\nKaiki bas\n \n–\n \nGoodbye\n \n(if we’re the one leaving) / Adiós (si somos nosotros los que nos vamos)\n\nKaiki bas!\n \n–\n \nWatch out! Be careful!\n \n/ ¡Cuidado!\n \n¡Ten cuidado!\n\nBas\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nboss, employer\n \n/\n \njefe, empleador\n\n(\nConstruct:\n \nBaski\n;\n \nBaskam\n;\n \nBaska\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n04/20\n):\n \nYawan dîa daukaia sip sa wan baska kum ba kupia swapni apia sa kaka?\n \n–\n \nWhat are we able to do if our boss\n\nis not reasonable?\n \n/\n \n¿Qué podemos hacer si tu jefe no es razonable?\n)\n\nBasil\n \n(\nbc\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nbasil\n \n/ albahaca\n\nBaskit\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbasket\n \n/ cesta\n\nBastar\n \n(\ndb,dict,dictu\n;\n \nBastard\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n) (n\n/s,adj)\n \n–\n \nillegitimate child, bastard, illegitimate\n \n/ hijo ilegítimo, bastardo,\n\nilegítimo\n\nBatakaia\n \n(v-trans)\n \n–\n \nto knock down, to throw down, to cause to fall down, to drop\n \n/ derribar, tirar, hacer caer, dejar caer\n\n(Ex/Ej\n \n(\nlfb18\n):\n \nBatakan taim, kînka ba piuta kum takan!\n \n–\n \nWhen he threw it down, the stick became a snake!\n \n/ Cuando lo tiró, ¡el\npalo se convirtió en una serpiente!)\n\nKupia batakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto knock down the heart, to discourage, to disappoint\n \n/ derribar el corazón, desalentar,\ndesanimar, decepcionar\n\nMina batakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stumble\n \n/ tropezar\n\nTukbi batakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto push and knock down\n \n/ empujar y derribar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb49\n):\n \nJehú adar\n \nyan: “T\nukbi bataks!\n”\n \n–\n \nJehu ordered: “Push (her) down!”\n \n/ Jehu ordenó: \"¡Empújala!\")\n\nBatana\n \n(n/s,adj)\n \n–\n \nfat, oil, grease, lard, fat\n \n(adj) / grasa, aceite, manteca de cerdo, gordo (adj)\n\n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAil\n)\n\n(Construct:\n \nBatanki\n;\n \nBatankam\n;\n \nBatanka\n)\n\nBatana laikaia\n \n(v) (\ndb-Aiseya 45:1\n; not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\n \ndictu\n)\n \n–\n \nto pour oil, to anoint\n \n/ verter aceite, ungir\n\nBatana laikan\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado, adj)\n \n–\n \nanointed\n \n/ ungió, ungido\n\n(Ex/Ej\n \n(\nmwb-02/19\n):\n \nBatana laikan kristianka nani ba Kraist ra hilp munbia Sitan uplika nani ra sauhki tikaia\ndukiara\n \n–\n \nAnointed Christians will help Christ to destroy Satan’s people\n \n/ Los cristianos ungidos ayudarán a Cristo\na destruir al pueblo de Satanás)\n\nKristian batana laikan ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nanointed Christian\n \n/ Cristiano ungido\n \n(a/t:\n \nSpirit ni laikan\nkristian\n;\n \nBatana laikan kristian\n;\n \nBâk sakan uplika nani; Bâk sakan kristianka nani\n)\n\nBatana laya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \noil\n \n/\n \naceite\n\nBatana laya watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \noil jar\n \n/\n \ntarro de aceite\n\nBatana yûkaia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nto anoint\n \n/ ungir\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1 King Nani 1:34\n):\n \nBahara prîs Sadoc bara prapit Natán bui Salaman ra batana yûkbia\n \n–\n \nThere priest Zadok and\nthe prophet Nathan will anoint Solomon\n \n/ Allí el sacerdote Sadoc y el profeta Natán ungirán a Salomón)\n\nBatanira\n \n(\ndb,dictu\n;\n \nBatanirra\n-\ndict\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nfat\n \n/ gordo\n\nBatankaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nBatanwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto fatten\n \n/ engordar\n\nBatanwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nBatankaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be fat, to become fat\n \n/ ser gordo, engordarse\n\nBatil\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbottle\n \n/ botella\n\nBatri\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbattery\n \n/ batería\n\nBatu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncanoa\n \n/ canoe\n\nBaul\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbowl\n \n/ tazón",
